Chapter 10: "The Land of the Lion King"
Chapter 10.9: "Crybaby"

――Felix Argyle.

He knew that was the real name of the person standing before him.

He'd heard it through others, and more than anything, the person himself had just announced it. Despite his delicate appearance, Subaru had once thought the name had a rather manly ring to it.

But even with him, who had just introduced himself by that name, standing right there, Subaru couldn't quite reconcile that fact with the reality before him.

That was how much the way this person lived was built upon the image of his nickname, "Ferris."

"Relieved of duty as a Knight...? That means..."

"It means I got fired, nya. Well, I guess it can't be helped. From the moment I decided to take that hand... to have the Divine Dragon Church save Lady Crusch... I was prepared for this. Ah, but please don't feel responsible, Emilia-sama."

"Ferris..."

"When you all came back then, it really gave me strength. Knowing that besides me and Old Man Wilhem, and others on Lady Crusch's side, there were people happy for her safety... It made me feel like what I did wasn't wrong after all."

Felis folded the cat ears on his head and answered, the corners of his eyes softening.

Hearing that answer, Emilia, who had stopped mid-step on her way to him, raised and lowered her hands as if unsure how to respond. Her confusion and bewilderment were natural.――However, looking at Felis in his tailcoat, casually claiming he'd resigned as a knight, Subaru's reaction was different.

"Wait! Subaru-kun, where are you going?"

"――Tch, where else? To see Crusch. This is too much."

Clenching his teeth, Subaru was about to turn on his heel when his back was called out to, and he raised his voice lowly.

He could guess the situation. To remove the "Dragon's Blood"侵蚀ing Crusch's body, they'd sought the help of the Divine Dragon Church. As a result, Crusch's camp's position in the Royal Selection had become precarious. And that decision had been made by Ferris, in place of the delirious Crusch.

It was Ferris's judgment that saved Crusch, but it made victory in the Royal Selection difficult. Even if that might not have been the choice of Crusch, who had a strong motivation to become king.

"But it was all for Crusch's sake, wasn't it? Yet firing you... that's just wrong!"

"Subaru!"

Beatrice, whose hand had been freed from Subaru's grip, cried out at his uncontrollable anger.

But Subaru didn't stop. He intended to run straight back to the Karsten mansion and confront Crusch herself, if necessary, to make her rescind her treatment of Ferris.

However, before he could take that first step, someone spread their arms and blocked his path――it was Rem.

"Rem, don't stop me. I don't want you all to see me yelling emotionally."

"If you're aware you're being overly emotional, then stop right there. Besides, before you go running off like that, why not properly look at the other person's face?"

"The other person's... face?"

Stopped in his tracks by Rem, Subaru nodded and then jerked his chin. Following the gesture, Subaru turned and saw Emilia and Beatrice looking at him worriedly, and beyond them, Felis looking down at him from the entrance of the mausoleum.

Felis, the very cause of Subaru's anger, looked exasperated at Subaru's outburst. He first turned his gaze towards Rem and said,

"Thanks, Rem-chan... It's my first time seeing you up and walking around, but you're a much better girl than I thought. Though, maybe your eye for men is lacking?"

"...I heard I was also in your care, Felis-san, while I was asleep. Because you're such a benefactor, I'll answer modestly... but that's a terrible misunderstanding."

"I see. If that's how you see it, Rem-chan, then it's fine. But, I'm glad you woke up."

Rem and Felis exchanged words over Subaru, who was caught between them. At that, Rem pursed her lips with a complicated expression, and then Felis switched gears with a "Well then."

He looked down at Subaru, narrowing his eyes.

"Subaru-kun, you're really arrogant, aren't you?"

"Arroga...?!"

"I'm choosing my words carefully here, you know? It's not like you're being selfish... you're doing it for someone else, not yourself. But it backfires something fierce, or rather, it's just meddling."

"You... saying that..."

"――And, I thought, if Subaru-kun is arrogant, then maybe I am too, nya."

At that moment, seeing that smile, Subaru felt as if he'd been doused with cold water.

"――――"

He caught his breath and stared back at Felis, who had just as harshly criticized himself as he had Subaru. Felis's demeanor hadn't changed since he'd noticed them at the mausoleum; he was still elusive, or rather, seemed far too composed to Subaru.

It was like a tranquil, calm sea.――But that couldn't be. Considering what had happened to Felis, he should be in the middle of a raging storm, not a calm sea.

Subaru focused his eyes, trying to find any sign of that storm in Felis's expression. But Felis, seemingly uninterested, winked one eye and then let out an "Ah," as if remembering something.

"That's right. If you'd like, Emilia-sama, why don't you all pay your respects too?"

"Pay respects...? You mean, inside the mausoleum behind you? Can we go in?"

"Yes, I have the key from the caretaker, and besides, I have the qualifications of a proxy visitor, so I come here quite often."

"Proxy visitor...?"

"Wow, Subaru-kun, you really don't know much, do you? Being her 'First Knight' like that, you might embarrass Emilia-sama, you know?"

Felis chuckled softly and stuck out his tongue, and Subaru fell silent.

Not because he was being called ignorant, but because hearing the term "First Knight" from Felis's mouth felt incredibly sensitive given the current situation.

Of course, the mischievous glint in Felis's eyes suggested he'd said it deliberately.

Toying with them like that, Felis gently placed his hand on the door of the mausoleum, which was just closing after he'd exited.

"Let's have our talk, all of it, inside.――I was just thinking His Highness might be lonely with only me visiting."

△▼△▼△▼△

Within the Royal Cemetery, the presence of this mausoleum was clearly distinct from the others.

Built from the finest white marble selected from across the kingdom, the structure was adorned everywhere with dragon motifs, the symbol of the Dragon Kingdom. It possessed a grandeur that overwhelmed any onlooker. Its outer walls, reflecting sunlight, radiated a holiness that seemed to repel evil, and the dragon statue that completed the closed door like a single painting appeared to eternally guard the dignity of the deceased royalty.

Stepping inside, the tombstones of the sleeping royalty lined the white corridors. The sarcophagi, arranged in perfect order, were each carved and decorated according to the individual royal, and just looking at them made the departed's life seem to rise before your eyes.

The tomb of the Fourth Prince, their destination, was especially evocative.

"This is His Highness's... Fourier Lugunica-sama's grave."

On the polished floor, Felis, who had been leading them with echoing footsteps, stopped and gestured towards a particularly prominent tombstone――Fourier Lugunica's sarcophagus.

Within the mausoleum, guarded by a strict, solemn order, that order seemed to waver slightly here.

After all, the Fourth Prince's tombstone was far too colorful for a resting place of the dead.

"Are these offerings? Letters, knitted goods, and wooden animal carvings..."

"None of them really look like offerings for royalty, do they? Actually, the people who asked for these things to be offered weren't really familiar with that kind of high-society etiquette, so I guess it can't be helped."

"People not familiar with it... you don't mean, these are gifts from common citizens? Wouldn't things like that be censored or confiscated when brought in?"

"Of course, if they were bad jokes, they wouldn't be allowed through. But I make sure they aren't when I receive them as a proxy visitor."

Kneeling before the sarcophagus, Felis narrowed his eyes at the various items placed there as he answered.

These offerings were probably prepared by those who admired the Fourth Prince resting here, each putting their own feelings into them, regardless of their social standing.

A proxy visitor was someone with special permission from the cemetery's caretaker to bring in such offerings on behalf of those who couldn't visit this place directly. Felis had been entrusted with people's feelings as a proxy visitor for this Fourth Prince.

"Originally, the Lugunica royals were all... well, good-natured, I guess? Kind and skilled at getting people to dote on them. But Prince Fourier was especially bright and had a cheerful personality. He'd often sneak out of the castle and go play with the people in the capital."

"...That's amazing. You hear stories like that in manga sometimes. But doing that for real would cause a huge commotion, wouldn't it?"

"Well, it did. They'd mobilize the royal guard to search for the missing prince. Once, they found him joining a soup kitchen in the slums, and because it was run by the Divine Dragon Church, it almost caused friction between the castle and the church. Big trouble."

"That's not something you can just laugh off as a joke now, is it?"

Looking past Felis's hunched back at the tombstone of Fourier, loved by so many, Subaru listened. Felis's nostalgic reminiscences were filled with undisguised affection for Fourier, the subject of the stories. Even from these snippets, you could tell he was a person loved by everyone.

"...Have I ever told you about the Prince before, Subaru-kun?"

"...Ah, that there was someone like that, and that he was close to you and Crusch-san. Did you also mention that he and I were a bit alike?"

"Huh? Why would I compare His Highness to Subaru-kun? I'll kill you, you know?"

"You said something similar back then too!!"

His voice had taken on a rather serious edge, so Subaru hurriedly clarified.

In truth, that was about the extent of what Subaru had been told about Fourier. Of course, even the slow-witted Subaru could understand that the person's death was not unrelated to Crusch's motivation for joining the Royal Selection.

"So, did Crusch-san join the Royal Selection for that Prince Fourier's sake?"

"...As expected from Emilia-sama. You really cut straight to the heart of the matter, even when it's hard to ask."

"Ah, I'm sorry. But you invited us to visit the grave because you wanted to tell us about it, right, Ferris? I want to hear it, and then decide what I should do next."

"Decide what to do next? What do you mean?"

"Yes. Subaru stole my thunder earlier, but I was also thinking of going to ask Crusch-san to reconsider. Subaru and I will talk to her together. How does that sound?"

"I think that's a good idea... Ow, ow ow!"

The moment he agreed with Emilia, Rem pinched his side, making him writhe in pain. "Please don't speak so impulsively. Do you realize where we are?" Seeing their reaction, Felis gave a wry smile and stood up.

"Like I said before, I'd really rather you didn't go saying things to Lady Crusch. I did what I did from the beginning knowing this would happen."

"But..."

"It's something I've already accepted. I said I was relieved of duty, but actually, I was the one who said I no longer deserved to be by her side. Besides..."

He put a finger to his lips, pausing for a moment, then used that same finger to point at Emilia, then at Subaru in turn.

"If someone... the Council of Wise Men, or whoever... told you to reconsider your master-servant relationship with Subaru-kun, what would you do, Emilia-sama?"

"Huh? My relationship with Subaru is something I thought about very hard and decided on myself. So if someone told me something like that, I'd feel really annoyed and think, 'What's your problem?'... Ah."

"That's right. What you were just about to do, Emilia-sama, is exactly that."

Blatant, unnecessary meddling by an outsider. Explained so clearly by Felis, Emilia visibly drooped her shoulders in disappointment. Faced with that reaction, there was little joy in hearing Emilia say she wouldn't want anyone interfering in her relationship with Subaru. More than anything, this argument was effective not just for Emilia, but for Subaru as well.

Felis, surely aware of this, shrugged slightly at Subaru over Emilia's dispirited form.

"To answer your earlier question, Lady Crusch isn't that narrow-minded. So, Prince Fourier was just one reason for joining the Royal Selection."

"...But it's a reason too significant to ignore, right?"

"My, my, you're good at nitpicking. You've lost all your cuteness, Subaru-kun."

However, he didn't seem particularly stung by that, and continued.

"I won't deny it. The Prince's death was a truly huge event for Lady Crusch... and for me. We were deeply hurt, and cried enough for a lifetime. Well, I'm a crybaby, so I ended up crying a lot after that too."

"――――"

"Lady Crusch didn't show it outwardly, but she was hurt, so hurt, and she suffered.――But the time Lady Crusch was hurt the most was after the Prince died."

"Huh..."

"The Prince, and then other royals, one after another passed away, and everyone was in chaos. Lady Crusch, as Duchess Karsten, attended council meetings at the castle as one of the high-ranking nobles... and that's when she realized. Everyone at those meetings was more worried about the possible severance of the pact with the Divine Dragon than about the royals' deaths."

It was a quiet way of speaking, carefully trying not to inject emotion. But that effort反而 highlighted the grotesqueness of the facts Felis was revealing.

Just by looking at this mausoleum, you could understand how warm and beloved the Lugunica royals were. Every tombstone, not just Fourier Lugunica's, had offerings praying for the peace of the departed soul.

Even the deaths of people so loved were trivialized before the pact with the Dragon.

"So that's why."

The whisper, barely a breath, came from Emilia, who had reached the same understanding as Subaru. She placed a hand on her chest and narrowed her violet-blue eyes sadly.

"So that's why Crusch-san decided that when she became king, she would make the country stronger, not one so dependent on the pact with the Dragon."

"――That's not all, but... yes, that's right."

"'Not all'... meaning?"

"Lady Crusch... really hated it. The thought that if she hadn't been close to Prince Fourier, she probably would have thought the same as everyone else."

There was no way to know that without experiencing it, and since it was something that could never happen, there was no reason for Crusch to blame herself. No matter what, Crusch had met Fourier and arrived at her convictions. Hating a version of herself that never existed would only bring pain.

But at the same time, Subaru realized that Crusch's situation wasn't simply about making a choice that contradicted her stance in the Royal Selection.

Crusch, who had declared she would end the pact with the Dragon, had been saved by borrowing the power of a sacrament from the Divine Dragon Church, which worshipped that very Dragon.――But it wasn't just that.

"Crusch-san vowed to restore a world where the Lugunica royals... where Prince Fourier could be genuinely mourned. She tried to fulfill that, but now she can't."

"...And on top of that, the Divine Dragon Church didn't save the Prince. But Lady Crusch saved you."

"――!"

Those faint words from Felis truly struck Subaru and the others' hearts.

Just moments ago, Subaru had been fully intent on arguing that relieving Ferris of his knighthood, even considering Crusch's poor physical and mental state, was too harsh.

But now, knowing that the resolve, determination, ideals, and vows Crusch carried had been shattered in the worst possible way, what could Subaru possibly say to her?

If only Subaru had offered his arm, his leg, anything, to take on Crusch's curse instead――

"See, that's why I said you're arrogant, Subaru-kun."

"Wha..."

"Anyone can see it from your face. No wonder Beatrice-chan can't let go of your hand. And while it might be a little better than nothing, you know it wouldn't solve anything, right?"

Felis's tone, tilting his head as if reasoning with a child, gently admonished the shallowness of Subaru's thoughts without being emotional about it.

He knew. Subaru's current thought was just an armchair theory, meaningless as Felis said.

Even if the one saved was Natsuki Subaru, Emilia's knight, instead of the Divine Dragon Church, Crusch would still be at a disadvantage for relying on an opposing camp to solve her problem. And in the Royal Selection, already past its midpoint, that was far too great a handicap.

"Asking outsiders to solve your own problems... that's not fit for a king, I guess..."

"――. Harsh, nya. But, that's it."

"...I'm just repeating what I heard."

And it was something he'd heard from none other than Crusch herself.

Back when the Witch Cult targeted Emilia, and Subaru asked Crusch for help without any bargaining chip, Crusch had cuttingly dismissed Subaru's ugly plea with dignity. That was a lesson Subaru was meant to learn. So he didn't resent Crusch for it. He didn't resent her, yet to have it thrown back at him like this was just too ironic.

"Hey, Ferris, I don't know if I should ask this..."

With Subaru silent and looking down, Emilia spoke to Felis in his place.

She stepped forward next to Felis, stood before Fourier Lugunica's tombstone, gazed at the many offerings placed there, then grasped the magic crystal on her chest and closed her eyes.

Looking behind her, Subaru saw Beatrice and Rem also offering their own silent prayers for the departed.

After finishing, Emilia looked at a particularly vibrant bouquet――the one Felis, crouching down, had just adjusted; probably brought by him――and asked.

"Were Crusch-san and Prince Fourier in love?"

"――――"

At that question, Felis's eyes widened slightly, and then he gave a small smile.

And then――,

"There's no way I could be the one to say that.――That would be far too insensitive."

